[size=5][b][color=#E8C88A]Combat Camera - Configurable[/color][/b][/size]

Choose a free camera, gentle target following or native tracking. Fight without a target, let your aim choose an enemy, or keep one enemy selected. Use your normal target-lock button to enter or leave targeting, and choose the locked behavior in Mod Setting Menu. Press Apply to use your settings straight away and keep them across save loads and game launches.

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Features[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Camera behavior:[/color][/b] Choose Free, Smooth tracking or Native tracking. Free is the default. Smooth follows your locked enemy horizontally and vertically, with adjustable speed and a pause after manual camera movement.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Disappearing enemies:[/color][/b] Smooth tracking can recover the same enemy when the game restores targeting after a temporary disappearance, even behind the camera. Works with fixed-target and camera-directed selection; unlocking cancels recovery.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Three targeting modes:[/color][/b] Select enemies by aiming the camera, keep one enemy selected, or fight with no target selected at all.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Aim unlocked attacks:[/color][/b] Attack toward the camera's horizontal aim even when the character faces elsewhere. Blocking still requires the correct incoming attack direction, without needing that enemy selected.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Optional center dot:[/color][/b] Choose Off, Weapon drawn, or Always in gameplay. Off is the default. The dot uses the game's HUD and hides during menus, cinematics and loading.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Controller aim slowdown:[/color][/b] Reduce right-stick camera sensitivity near your target during camera-directed targeting, with adjustable strength. Fixed-target and untargeted modes keep full sensitivity. It does not steer the camera, and mouse movement is excluded.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Saved settings:[/color][/b] Choose camera behavior, tracking speed, resume delay, targeting behavior, center dot and slowdown. Mod Setting Menu changes take effect when you press Apply and are restored on the next launch.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Installation[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Vortex:[/color][/b] Install Combat-Camera-Configurable.zip through Vortex, enable it and deploy.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Manual:[/color][/b] Copy the archive's Data/CombatCamera folder into The Blood of Dawnwalker/Dawnwalker/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/Mods, preserving the folder structure.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Configuration[/color][/b][/size]

Open Mod Settings, select [b]Combat Camera - Configurable[/b], adjust the controls and press [b]Apply[/b].

[list]
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Enable mod:[/color][/b] On by default.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Camera behavior:[/color][/b] Free by default. Smooth tracking gently follows a locked enemy; Native tracking uses the game's normal tracking speed.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Tracking speed:[/color][/b] 50% by default, adjustable from 10% to 100%. Controls smooth following independently of controller aim slowdown.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Tracking resume delay:[/color][/b] 750 ms (0.75 seconds) by default, adjustable from 0 to 3000 ms. Smooth tracking yields immediately to mouse or right-stick movement, then eases back in after this pause.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Camera-directed targeting:[/color][/b] On selects enemies toward the camera while locked. Off retains your chosen enemy. Both choices work with all three camera behaviors.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Target switch delay:[/color][/b] 65 ms by default; adjustable from 0 to 1000 ms.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Targeting cone:[/color][/b] 45° from the camera axis by default; adjustable from 1° to 90°. Set 0 to use the native cone.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Center dot:[/color][/b] Off by default. Other choices are Weapon drawn and Always in gameplay.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Controller aim slowdown:[/color][/b] On by default.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Slowdown strength:[/color][/b] 35% by default; adjustable from 0% to 80%.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Logging:[/color][/b] Off by default. When enabled, writes Apply events and aggregate diagnostics to Dawnwalker/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/UE4SS.log.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Targeting behavior[/color][/b][/size]

Press [b]R3 / right-stick click[/b], or your configured keyboard/controller [b]target-lock[/b] binding, to enter or leave targeting. Camera behavior is independent of these targeting states:

[list=1]
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Camera-directed targeting:[/color][/b] Target lock On, Camera-directed targeting On. Aim the camera toward an enemy to select them. Adjust the targeting cone and switch delay to control how selection responds.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Fixed enemy selection:[/color][/b] Target lock On, Camera-directed targeting Off. Keep your chosen enemy selected. Smooth tracking temporarily yields when you look around. To choose someone else, unlock, aim toward the new enemy and lock again.
[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Untargeted combat:[/color][/b] Target lock Off, with either targeting setting. No enemy is automatically selected. Attack in the direction your camera is facing.
[/list]

Both locked modes keep their target-based attack direction. Moving the right stick or mouse controls the camera and does not cycle a fixed target. Applying camera or targeting settings preserves your current lock state. Leaving combat or loading a new player starts untargeted.

Automatic targeting runs only while target lock and Camera-directed targeting are both on. It shares a 50 ms minimum interval between full native selection passes. A fallback search waits until the next interval, while a single-target validity check can retain the current target. The game still handles eligibility, visibility and combat targeting rules. Settings are read at startup and updated through Apply, without repeated INI polling.

[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Credits and source[/color][/b][/size]

Inspired by [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/340]Free Combat Camera – Camera Directed Targeting[/url] by xxxxxMIKxxxxx. [b]This is an independent implementation: no code from the original mod was copied or reused.[/b] The original mod is not required, and its DLL, configuration and bootstrap are not included.

Thanks to the UE4SS contributors, Framecore, mmarcussa for Mod Setting Menu, and Tsuda Kageyu and contributors for MinHook.

